      "quote_britannica": "It is mainly cut with the reproduction of eggs and anchors or arrows heads placed alternately.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The \"egg and tongue\" referred to, also known as egg-and-dart, egg-and-anchor, or egg-and-star, refers to alternating egg and V-shapes enriching the surface of the concave ovolo in many early cases."
    }
  ],
  "wiki_only_topics": [
    {
      "topic": "Etymology of the word ovolo",
      "quote_wikipedia": "Ovolo is an Italian word that means \"little egg\"."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Comparison with cavetto and compound moldings",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The fundamental element of ornamental, architectural molding that is concave (rather than convex like the ovolo) is found in cavetto or hollow chamfering moldings, which also usually presents a quarter-round cross-section, albeit concave."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Modern residential applications of ovolo",
      "quote_wikipedia": "In modern residential applications, the ovolo profile is often used as the inside edge of stile and rail interior and cabinet doors."
    }
  ]
}
